const luxuryNarrative = {
  headline: 'From Pelican Hill Gates to Balboa Island Galleys',
  paragraphs: [
    "Newport Beach luxury comes in two grains. On the gated coast — Newport Coast, Pelican Hill, Crystal Cove — the houses are newer and the suites are complete: Sub-Zero columns, Wolf ranges, Gaggenau and Miele designed in from the first drawing. Down on the harbor the geometry flips: Balboa Island and Peninsula lots are tight, and the same brands get packaged into compact, panel-ready configurations that leave no slack for service access.",
    "We plan for both before dispatch — gate and HOA coordination for the coast, parking and access planning for the island streets — with the full brand set's OEM parts on the Orange County truck before it leaves. Two hundred feet from the ocean, the salt clock this page describes is already running on everything we put a part into."
  ]
};

